{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md","content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT (re-review round 2 — still present at this line): the task-ledger record bypasses the redaction pipeline**

The rework round pushed no commits (only `main` merge refreshes), so this thread from the first review remains open and still reproduces at `trajectory_commands.dart:173`:

```dart
data: event.ledger.toJson(),
```

Every free-text field in the record (`requirement`, `command`, `expected`, `actual`) is agent-authored text — and the FinalizeGate contract + `credentialHuntNudge` actively direct the agent to probe credential locations (`~/.aws/`, `~/.ssh/`, `~/.git-credentials`, env) and record verification commands and their observed output in these very fields.

The repo's own convention (gh-1054 review, `_persistToolLivenessRecord` in `agent_cli_persist.dart`) is explicit:

> Free-text fields ... pass through the host's redaction pipeline first: the session JSONL is an audit surface and must not leak secrets the in-run hooks already mask elsewhere.

The `task_ledger` record is an audit surface three times over: it lands in the session JSONL, is broadcast to external hosts via the `task_ledger` wire frame, and is synced into bench trial dirs (`agent-logs/fah-sessions`). Suggested fix, mirroring the sibling persister:

```dart
Future<void> _onTaskLedger(TaskLedgerEvent event) async {
  final session = _session;
  if (session == null) return;
  final pipeline = config.redactionPipeline;
  final data = pipeline == null
      ? event.ledger.toJson()
      : {
          'items': [
            for (final item in event.ledger.items)
              {
                ...item.toJson(),
                'requirement': pipeline.redact(item.requirement),
                'command': pipeline.redact(item.command),
                'expected': pipeline.redact(item.expected),
                'actual': pipeline.redact(item.actual),
              },
          ],
        };
  try {
    await session.appendCustomEntry(customType: taskLedgerRecordType, data: data);
  } on Object catch (error) {
    io.writeln(tuiError('task ledger persist failed: $error'));
  }
}
```

The in-run hooks usually mask secrets before the model sees them, so this is defense-in-depth — but it is exactly the class of record gh-1054 added the convention for, and the sibling liveness persister already pays this cost. A regression test mirroring the liveness redaction test would pin it.
"}

